  "faqs": [
    {
      "question": "What is a credit?",
      "answer": "One credit is worth $0.01. Credits pay for Agenta's built-in models and for sandbox time, the time an agent runs in a sandbox that Agenta hosts."
    },
    {
      "question": "How many credits does each plan include?",
      "answer": "Every new organization gets $5 of credits (500 credits) at signup. Hobby also gets 75 free credits every day. Daily credits reset at midnight UTC and do not roll over. Pro includes 2,900 credits every month and Business includes 29,900 credits every month. Monthly credits expire at the end of the billing period."
    },
    {
      "question": "How much does an agent use?",
      "answer": "Built-in models cost the provider's list price times 1.75. Sandbox time costs Daytona's list price times 3, or times 2.5 on Business. When an agent uses your own provider key, the model costs no credits and only sandbox time is charged."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is a trace?",
      "answer": "A trace is the record Agenta creates for each agent run so you can inspect its model calls, tool calls, timing, outputs, and errors. Sending a message to an agent, creating an annotation, or starting an agent from a schedule or event each creates one trace."
    },
    {
      "question": "Are users, projects, agents, and workflows really unlimited?",
      "answer": "Yes, on every paid Cloud plan and both self-hosted plans. Invite as many team members as you need and create as many projects, agents, workflows, schedules, and triggers as you want. The free Cloud Hobby plan includes two team members. You pay for credits and traces, not for seats, projects, agents, steps, or workflows."
    },
    {
      "question": "Are AI model costs included?",
      "answer": "Agenta's built-in models are paid with credits. You can also connect your own model-provider credentials and pay the provider directly. Then the model costs no credits, and only sandbox time is charged."
    },
    {
      "question": "Which model providers can I use?",
      "answer": "Connect OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Mistral, Groq, MiniMax, Together AI, OpenRouter, Azure OpenAI, AWS Bedrock, or Google Vertex AI. You can also connect an OpenAI-compatible endpoint."
    },
    {
      "question": "What happens when I run out of credits?",
      "answer": "New requests do not start until you have credits again. Requests that are already running finish. On Hobby, your free daily credits come back at midnight UTC. On Pro and Business, you can buy more credits."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I buy more credits?",
      "answer": "Yes, on Pro and Business. $10 buys 1,000 credits, $25 buys 2,500 credits, and $100 buys 10,000 credits. Purchased credits expire after 12 months."
    },
    {
      "question": "How many agents can run at once, and for how long?",
      "answer": "Hobby runs 2 agents at once, and each request can run for up to 30 minutes. Pro runs 10 agents at once, for up to 4 hours per request. Business runs 25 agents at once, for up to 11 hours per request."
    },
    {
      "question": "What happens when I reach my trace limit?",
      "answer": "Hobby records up to 5,000 traces in a monthly billing period. After that, Agenta stops recording new traces until the next period. Pro and Business include 10,000 traces per month. Additional traces are billed automatically at $5 per 10,000."
    },
    {
      "question": "Where can I monitor usage?",
      "answer": "Open Settings, then Credits to see your credit balance and what used your credits. Open Settings, then Usage & Billing to see your plan and its limits."
    },
    {
      "question": "What does trace data retention cover?",
      "answer": "Trace data retention controls how long Agenta Cloud keeps technical execution records, including model calls, tool calls, timing, outputs, errors, evaluations, and annotations. Hobby retains trace data for one week, Pro for one month, and Business for three months. Enterprise retention is configurable. Trace data retention does not describe the retention of chats, project files, or persistent agent context. With self-hosted Agenta, you manage trace storage and retention in your own infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the difference between Agenta Cloud and self-hosted Agenta?",
      "answer": "Agenta Cloud is operated by us. We run the application, storage, agent runner, upgrades, and backups. With self-hosted Agenta, you deploy and operate those components in your own infrastructure, connect your own model and integration accounts, and control where your data is stored."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is included in the free open-source edition?",
      "answer": "The open-source edition includes the core agent workspace: chat, projects, agent configuration, instructions, skills, tools, integrations, MCP servers, files, schedules, event triggers, tracing, evaluations, version history, role-based access control, and SSO. You can create unlimited users, projects, agents, and workflows on your own infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "question": "Why pay for Enterprise if Agenta is open source?",
      "answer": "Enterprise adds audit logs, custom domains, deployment and upgrade support, priority support, a private Slack Connect channel, dedicated support, and a custom service-level agreement. The open-source edition remains free for teams that can operate it themselves and do not need those commercial features or services."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I switch plans or cancel at any time?",
      "answer": "Yes. Upgrade, downgrade, or cancel from Settings, then Billing."
    },
    {
      "question": "Do you offer discounts for startups, students, or researchers?",
      "answer": "Yes. Early-stage startups, students, and researchers can email team@agenta.ai to ask about discounted or free access. Include what you are building and how you plan to use Agenta."
    }
  ]
}
